 usic\, Jazz\nCategories: concert\, free\nSource: ticketmaster/music\n\nSpe
 ncer Day Feinstein's at the Nikko November 20 & 21 Previewing his new Proj
 ect: La Frontera Spencer Day comes home to San Francisco for the first liv
 e preview of La Frontera\, his exciting new collection of original music i
 nspired by his life in Mexico. Blending jazz\, pop\, the Great American So
 ngbook and Latin influences\, Spencer explores the cultural connections be
 tween Mexico and the U.S.---and the unexpected ways music can bring us tog
 ether. This special evening will feature brand-new songs and arrangements 
 from La Frontera alongside favorites from Spencer's celebrated catalog\, p
 lus a very special guest musician from Mexico. With his signature mix of s
 ophisticated musicianship\, storytelling and humor\, Spencer invites audie
 nces to be among the first to experience where his music is headed next. A
  new chapter. A special homecoming. A first listen. Don't miss Spencer Day
  at Feinstein's at the Nikko. From the Artist \, "rdquo" -> I've spent the
  last few years falling ever deeper in love with Mexico---not just with th
 e music\, but with the people\, the culture and the way so many of our tra
 ditions coexist\," says Day. \, "rdquo" -> La Frontera grew out of that ex
 perience. It's about more than just the border---it's about what happens w
 hen cultures meet\, influence one another and create something new. It's a
  meditation on the many things that connect us and divide us. I'm incredib
 ly excited to share it for the first time with the city that gave me my st
 art. San Francisco has always 
LOCATION:222 Mason Street\, San Francisco\, CA
URL:https://www.ticketweb.com/event/spencer-day-la-frontera-premier-feinst
 eins-at-the-nikko-tickets/15019983
